gue’s platform or ESPN with valid authentication. Local games (Prime Video): Prime Video (in-market only): The platform will exclusively stream 21 Yankees games this year under a partnership with YES Network. Available for $15/month. More information about local Yankees broadcasts can be found here. National games: Peacock: All NBC Sports-produced games on the NBC broadcast network and Peacock. ESPN Unlimited: All ESPN-produced games on the ESPN cable networks and ABC, plus the ability to purchase MLB.TV as an add-on subscription. Disney+: Occasional simulcasts of ESPN-produced games. Apple TV: All “Friday Night Baseball” games throughout the season. HBO Max: All TNT Sports-produced games on the TBS cable network. Fox One: All Fox Sports-produced games on the Fox broadcast network and FS1. Netflix: Access to watch Opening Night, the Home Run Derby and the MLB at Field of Dreams Game. Team Total ABC Apple TV ESPN Fox FS1 MLB Network NBC Netflix Peacock TBS New York Yankees 26 1 1 1 7 1 5 3 1 1 5 Cable and Streaming Bundles YouTube TV: All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC, Fox/FS1 and TBS. Some Peacock-exclusive games will be available via NBCSN. (Peacock can also be purchased in full through YouTube Channels). Sponsored offer: Get $75 off YouTube TV ($15 off for 5 months) when you sign up today. New users only. Cancel Anytime. Terms apply. Sling: All games on ESPN/ABC (ABC games will be on ESPN3), Fox/FS1, NBC and TBS. Fubo: All games on ESPN/ABC and Fox/FS1. DIRECTV (stream): All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC, Fox/FS1 and TBS. Linear cable (ex. Dish Network, Xfinity, DIRECTV): All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC and Fox/FS1. Hulu + Live TV: All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC, Fox/FS1 and TBS. In-Person See the Yankees in person at Yankee Stadium, or catch Major League Baseball games from any of the 30 ballparks this season, by purchasing tickets through Vivid Seats, SeatGeek or Gametime.",
